        "titulo": "The scissors rule of the prepositional",
        "explicacao": "The scissors rule of the prepositional. Now the mechanics. How does the noun change when it goes into the prepositional? The scissors work as always: • 1. Find the nominative form (the dictionary word). • 2. Apply the prepositional ending, which depends on the gender and on the ending. • 3. Done. The noun is in the prepositional. Look at the endings in the table. Notice that the rule is almost always -Е. Only feminine nouns in -ь and nouns in -ия/-ие take -И (written -ИИ for those in -ия/-ие). And neuter nouns in -мя take -ЕНИ. Let's look at each case in detail.",
