        "titulo": "The neuter and the master table of the prepositional",
        "explicacao": "The NEUTER in the prepositional. The neuter is the simplest. Two rules. Neuter in -о: notice that the -о becomes -е. Always. Neuter in -е: words in -е usually stay the same. But words in -ие (with an \"i\" before the \"e\") get -ии: упражне́ние → упражне́нии, зна́ние → зна́нии, зда́ние → зда́нии. Why? The same logic as -ия → -ии. Neuter in -мя → ending -ЕНИ. Neuter words ending in -мя get -ени. There are about 10 of them, and you already know them from lesson 11. They are neuter and end in -мя. In the prepositional they become -мени. The master table of the prepositional. Here is the table that solves everything.",
